{"ts": "2026-10-20T11:03:40.230871Z", "run_id": "r-20261020T1103Z-1817", "unit": "kiro:tenant-scoped-core", "seq": 10, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-005", "target": "C-7881686c", "decision": "accept", "by": "human", "reason": "verified on the unit branch: MCP memory_dream (server.py), CLI dream (main.py) and HTTP POST /dream (app.py, importing run_dream as run_tenant_dreams) each call run_dream(store, intensity=..., tenant_id=None, engine_factory=...); MCP and CLI build engines with build_dreaming_engine(store, settings.llm, link_settings=settings.link, summary_settings=settings.summary, tenant_id=t), the API with DreamingEngine(store, tenant_id=t). The three transport tests that trace it pass.", "text_sha256": "035110f2abcb890d1e689a0b16a06ef61b41255b2d4c623acd0f3bc75bea4248", "answer_sha256": "95b8d4174cb6dbc904f5329dc3d7bb24541c78b1e0808c307d341f512647e843"}
{"ts": "2026-10-20T11:03:40.232524Z", "run_id": "r-20261020T1103Z-1817", "unit": "kiro:tenant-scoped-core", "seq": 11, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-006", "target": "C-d9c39ea3", "decision": "accept", "by": "human", "reason": "verified on the unit branch: run_dream returns a DreamReport (one tenant's, or DreamAllReport.total() for the global scope, the per-tenant total); MCP returns report.model_dump(mode='json'), the CLI prints the DreamReport table, the API route has response_model=DreamReport (its test parses the body as DreamReport).", "text_sha256": "fe5621057b87c316ec575a8ea67ea3737d682d7f5c9316501029ae42f91e99ea", "answer_sha256": "4db9e4abf1e2c78286d5f4348628a2d6fb02f52d63d43e88b75f0819417b85d4"}
{"ts": "2026-10-20T11:03:40.233462Z", "run_id": "r-20261020T1103Z-1817", "unit": "kiro:tenant-scoped-core", "seq": 12, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-007", "target": "C-63860dbc", "decision": "accept", "by": "human", "reason": "verified on the unit branch: run_dream raises DreamFailedError when any tenant's pass fails; the CLI catches it and prints 'error: <message>' on stderr with exit code 1, the API's exception handler returns 500 {'detail': str(exc)}, and the MCP tool lets it propagate so the fastmcp client gets a ToolError (test_memory_dream_failure_surfaces_as_a_tool_error passes).", "text_sha256": "c623eb0ba8e69ad80b14d67c184dd28a61d6e90dc8d67833eedf9cf3928f0b55", "answer_sha256": "70f6ebe5e4997436de1f0593beafda8432967fd8e29d0944f0feb0949c1d7e7b"}
{"ts": "2026-10-20T11:03:40.234694Z", "run_id": "r-20261020T1103Z-1817", "unit": "kiro:tenant-scoped-core", "seq": 13, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-008", "target": "C-a0213e6c", "decision": "accept", "by": "human", "reason": "verified on the unit branch: MCP summary_jobs/summary_put, CLI summary-jobs/summary-put and HTTP GET /summaries/jobs and PUT /summaries/{concept} all build their engine with tenant_id=TENANT_GLOBAL, so on a multi-tenant database they see global memories only and on a one-tenant database (everything global) the output is unchanged; the three transport tests that trace it pass.", "text_sha256": "0381edf030d3a99f80b91da44641da0bb83b50c2ff8fced694e9b74081211b25", "answer_sha256": "d3c2a150d3e5a3113a94a0449b3c00aef6f873d984e56f4e9f1684b824f3b97b"}
